sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Cl as Client
    participant Ev as Event loop
    participant K as Kernel
    participant Disk as Storage
    Cl->>Ev: upload stream
    Ev->>K: readable event, non-blocking read
    K-->>Ev: a chunk
    Ev->>Disk: write it through, never buffer the whole object
    Note over Ev,Disk: bounded memory per connection is what lets one process hold thousands
    alt the client sends faster than disk accepts
        Ev->>Cl: stop reading — TCP backpressure slows the sender
        Note over Ev,Cl: backpressure, not an unbounded queue, is what stops the OOM
    end
    Cl->>Ev: download
    Ev->>K: sendfile — disk to socket without copying through user space
    K-->>Cl: bytes
